/* Verse Games: THE WHOLE COUNSEL · 1 Kings chapters 1-5
   Verse text is filled/verified from the KJV by tools/fill-verses.js */
VG.registerBibleChapters("1kings", [
{n:1, name:"Solomon Anointed King", seal:{ref:"1 Kings 1:39",verse:"And Zadok the priest took an horn of oil out of the tabernacle, and anointed Solomon. And they blew the trumpet; and all the people said, God save king Solomon."}, facts:["Did you know David's servants sought a fair young Shunammite, Abishag, to cherish the old king and give him warmth, yet the text notes plainly that the king knew her not (1 Kings 1:4)?","Did you know Adonijah copied Absalom's playbook, preparing chariots and horsemen with fifty men to run before him before he ever asked his father (1 Kings 1:5)?","Did you know Solomon was anointed king at Gihon, not in the palace, and the people piped with pipes and rejoiced with such joy that the earth rent with the sound of them (1 Kings 1:39-40)?"], questions:[
{q:"How is old King David described as the chapter opens?", options:["Old and stricken in years; they covered him with clothes, but he gat no heat","Strong and riding out to battle","Sleeping soundly through the day","Blind and unable to speak"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 1:1",verse:"Now king David was old and stricken in years; and they covered him with clothes, but he gat no heat.", insight:"Even kings grow cold with age; the mightiest strength runs out, and only God's warmth remains."},
{q:"What remedy did David's servants propose for his coldness?", options:["Seek a young virgin to stand before him, cherish him, and lie in his bosom","Carry him to a warmer land","Give him strong wine at every meal","Wrap him in plates of iron"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 1:2",verse:"Wherefore his servants said unto him, Let there be sought for my lord the king a young virgin: and let her stand before the king, and let her cherish him, and let her lie in thy bosom, that my lord the king may get heat.", insight:"Human fixes reach only so far; warmth borrowed from another cannot replace the fire within."},
{q:"Who was found and brought to the king?", options:["Abishag a Shunammite","Abigail the Carmelitess","Michal the daughter of Saul","Rizpah the daughter of Aiah"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 1:3",verse:"So they sought for a fair damsel throughout all the coasts of Israel, and found Abishag a Shunammite, and brought her to the king.", insight:"God lets the record show her name; the lowly who serve faithfully are remembered in Scripture."},
{q:"What did Adonijah the son of Haggith do?", options:["Exalted himself, saying, I will be king, and prepared chariots, horsemen, and fifty men to run before him","Asked David's blessing for the throne","Built an altar and prayed for guidance","Fled to Hebron to wait his turn"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 1:5",verse:"Then Adonijah the son of Haggith exalted himself, saying, I will be king: and he prepared him chariots and horsemen, and fifty men to run before him.", insight:"'I will be king' is the cry of every self-made crown; God's anointing is given, never seized."},
{q:"With whom did Adonijah confer?", options:["Joab the son of Zeruiah, and Abiathar the priest","Zadok the priest and Nathan the prophet","Benaiah and the mighty men","David and Bath-sheba"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 1:7",verse:"And he conferred with Joab the son of Zeruiah, and with Abiathar the priest: and they following Adonijah helped him.", insight:"Rebellion always finds counselors; check whose table you sit at before the feast begins."},
{q:"Who was not with Adonijah?", options:["Zadok the priest, Benaiah, Nathan the prophet, Shimei, Rei, and David's mighty men","Joab the captain of the host","Abiathar the priest","All his brethren, the king's sons"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 1:8",verse:"But Zadok the priest, and Benaiah the son of Jehoiada, and Nathan the prophet, and Shimei, and Rei, and the mighty men which belonged to David, were not with Adonijah.", insight:"The godly remnant refused the rebel's feast; not every invitation deserves your presence."},
{q:"Where did Adonijah hold his coronation feast?", options:["By the stone of Zoheleth, by En-rogel","At Gihon, by the spring","In the tabernacle court","On the Mount of Olives"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 1:9",verse:"And Adonijah slew sheep and oxen and fat cattle by the stone of Zoheleth, which is by En-rogel, and called all his brethren the king’s sons, and all the men of Judah the king’s servants:", insight:"He chose a famous stone for his feast; God would choose a spring at Gihon for the true crowning."},
{q:"Whom did Adonijah pointedly not invite?", options:["Nathan, Benaiah, the mighty men, and Solomon his brother","Joab the son of Zeruiah","Abiathar the priest","All the men of Judah"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 1:10",verse:"But Nathan the prophet, and Benaiah, and the mighty men, and Solomon his brother, he called not.", insight:"The guest list betrays the plot; whom you exclude says as much as whom you invite."},
{q:"Who warned Bath-sheba that Adonijah was reigning?", options:["Nathan the prophet","Zadok the priest","Benaiah the son of Jehoiada","Joab the captain"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 1:11",verse:"Wherefore Nathan spake unto Bath-sheba the mother of Solomon, saying, Hast thou not heard that Adonijah the son of Haggith doth reign, and David our lord knoweth it not?", insight:"God still has watchmen who speak in time; heed the Nathan who warns you."},
{q:"What was Bath-sheba to remind David he had sworn?", options:["Assuredly Solomon thy son shall reign after me, and he shall sit upon my throne","Adonijah should be made captain of the host","The temple must be built at once","Joab must be forgiven"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 1:13",verse:"Go and get thee in unto king David, and say unto him, Didst not thou, my lord, O king, swear unto thine handmaid, saying, Assuredly Solomon thy son shall reign after me, and he shall sit upon my throne? why then doth Adonijah reign?", insight:"Hold God's servants to their holy promises; a sworn oath before the LORD still binds."},
{q:"What did Bath-sheba fear if Adonijah kept the throne?", options:["She and Solomon would be counted offenders when David slept with his fathers","She would be sent back to Shunem","Solomon would be sold into Egypt","The temple would never be built"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 1:21",verse:"Otherwise it shall come to pass, when my lord the king shall sleep with his fathers, that I and my son Solomon shall be counted offenders.", insight:"Usurped power always hunts rivals; Bath-sheba saw clearly what the crown would cost her son."},
{q:"What did David swear to Bath-sheba?", options:["As the LORD liveth, Solomon thy son shall reign after me, and sit upon my throne in my stead, even so will I certainly do this day","Adonijah shall be spared and honored","The kingdom shall be divided in peace","No blood shall be shed in Israel"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 1:30",verse:"Even as I sware unto thee by the LORD God of Israel, saying, Assuredly Solomon thy son shall reign after me, and he shall sit upon my throne in my stead; even so will I certainly do this day.", insight:"David's oath was his anchor; when the king remembers his vow, the kingdom steadies."},
{q:"Whom did David summon to crown Solomon?", options:["Zadok the priest, Nathan the prophet, and Benaiah the son of Jehoiada","Joab, Abiathar, and Adonijah","The elders of Judah","The sons of the prophets"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 1:32",verse:"And king David said, Call me Zadok the priest, and Nathan the prophet, and Benaiah the son of Jehoiada. And they came before the king.", insight:"David chose the faithful, not the flatterers; surround your greatest moments with proven men."},
{q:"On what did David command Solomon to ride?", options:["David's own mule","A warhorse","A golden chariot","A camel from Egypt"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 1:33",verse:"The king also said unto them, Take with you the servants of your lord, and cause Solomon my son to ride upon mine own mule, and bring him down to Gihon:", insight:"The king's own mule was a public sign; true succession is seen, not whispered."},
{q:"Where was Solomon to be anointed?", options:["At Gihon","At En-rogel","In the tabernacle","In Hebron"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 1:34",verse:"And let Zadok the priest and Nathan the prophet anoint him there king over Israel: and blow ye with the trumpet, and say, God save king Solomon.", insight:"Gihon, the spring of living water; God loves to crown His kings beside flowing water."},
{q:"What did Zadok use to anoint Solomon?", options:["A horn of oil out of the tabernacle","A vial of perfume","A cup of spring water","Olive branches"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 1:39",verse:"And Zadok the priest took an horn of oil out of the tabernacle, and anointed Solomon. And they blew the trumpet; and all the people said, God save king Solomon.", insight:"Oil from the tabernacle, not from Adonijah's feast; God's appointments come from His house."},
{q:"How did the people celebrate Solomon's anointing?", options:["They piped with pipes, and rejoiced with great joy, so that the earth rent with the sound","They stood in solemn silence","They wept for the aging David","They marched out to battle"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 1:40",verse:"And all the people came up after him, and the people piped with pipes, and rejoiced with great joy, so that the earth rent with the sound of them.", insight:"Joy so loud it split the earth; when God establishes His king, gladness cannot be contained."},
{q:"How did the people celebrate Solomon's anointing?", options:["They piped with pipes and rejoiced with great joy, so that the earth rent with the sound","They wept in silence","They fled the city in fear","They armed themselves for war"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 1:40",verse:"And all the people came up after him, and the people piped with pipes, and rejoiced with great joy, so that the earth rent with the sound of them.", insight:"Joy that rents the earth is God's doing; heaven's choices bring earth's loudest praise."},
{q:"What did Adonijah do when he heard Solomon was king?", options:["He feared, arose, and caught hold on the horns of the altar","He fled to Egypt","He gathered an army","He hid in a cave"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 1:50",verse:"And Adonijah feared because of Solomon, and arose, and went, and caught hold on the horns of the altar.", insight:"The altar that rebels scorned became their refuge; even the proud run to mercy at last."},
{q:"What was Solomon's final word to Adonijah?", options:["Go to thine house","Thou art banished forever","Pay a ransom of gold","Serve in the temple"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 1:53",verse:"So king Solomon sent, and they brought him down from the altar. And he came and bowed himself to king Solomon: and Solomon said unto him, Go to thine house.", insight:"Mercy with a boundary: Solomon spared him, but sent him home. Grace is not permission."}
]},
{n:2, name:"David's Last Charge", seal:{ref:"1 Kings 2:3",verse:"And keep the charge of the LORD thy God, to walk in his ways, to keep his statutes, and his commandments, and his judgments, and his testimonies, as it is written in the law of Moses, that thou mayest prosper in all that thou doest, and whithersoever thou turnest thyself:"}, facts:["Did you know David reigned forty years in all, seven years in Hebron and thirty-three in Jerusalem, and was buried in the city of David (1 Kings 2:10-11)?","Did you know Solomon thrust Abiathar out of the priesthood, fulfilling the word of the LORD spoken against the house of Eli at Shiloh (1 Kings 2:27)?","Did you know Shimei broke his oath over two runaway servants, saddling his ass and riding to Gath to fetch them, and it cost him his life (1 Kings 2:39-40)?"], questions:[
{q:"How did David describe his own dying?", options:["I go the way of all the earth","I am lifted up to heaven","I fear the grave greatly","I shall see my father today"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 2:2",verse:"I go the way of all the earth: be thou strong therefore, and shew thyself a man;", insight:"'The way of all the earth' humbles every king; death is the one road no crown avoids."},
{q:"What was David's first charge to Solomon?", options:["Keep the charge of the LORD thy God, to walk in his ways and keep his statutes, commandments, judgments, and testimonies","Build the temple before anything else","Avenge all my enemies","Number the people of Israel"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 2:3",verse:"And keep the charge of the LORD thy God, to walk in his ways, to keep his statutes, and his commandments, and his judgments, and his testimonies, as it is written in the law of Moses, that thou mayest prosper in all that thou doest, and whithersoever thou turnest thyself:", insight:"A father's last word to a king was not about power but obedience; the throne stands on the law of God."},
{q:"What promise did David tie to keeping God's law?", options:["There shall not fail thee a man on the throne of Israel","Thy enemies shall never rise","Thou shalt reign a hundred years","The temple shall stand forever"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 2:4",verse:"That the LORD may continue his word which he spake concerning me, saying, If thy children take heed to their way, to walk before me in truth with all their heart and with all their soul, there shall not fail thee (said he) a man on the throne of Israel.", insight:"God's covenant keeps its shape through obedience; the dynasty depends on walking with God."},
{q:"Whose hoar head was not to go down to the grave in peace?", options:["Joab the son of Zeruiah","Abiathar the priest","Shimei the son of Gera","Adonijah the son of Haggith"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 2:6",verse:"Do therefore according to thy wisdom, and let not his hoar head go down to the grave in peace.", insight:"David had spared Joab too long; delayed justice is still justice, and it falls at last."},
{q:"What had Joab done to the two captains?", options:["He slew Abner and Amasa, shedding the blood of war in peace","He stole the ark of God","He cursed David at Bahurim","He joined Absalom's rebellion"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 2:5",verse:"Moreover thou knowest also what Joab the son of Zeruiah did to me, and what he did to the two captains of the hosts of Israel, unto Abner the son of Ner, and unto Amasa the son of Jether, whom he slew, and shed the blood of war in peace, and put the blood of war upon his girdle that was about his loins, and in his shoes that were on his feet.", insight:"Blood shed in peace stains the shedder; God remembers murders that men excuse."},
{q:"Whom was Solomon commanded to show kindness to?", options:["The sons of Barzillai the Gileadite","The sons of Eli","The household of Saul","The elders of Hebron"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 2:7",verse:"But shew kindness unto the sons of Barzillai the Gileadite, and let them be of those that eat at thy table: for so they came to me when I fled because of Absalom thy brother.", insight:"Kindness outlives the giver; David's gratitude reached past his grave to Barzillai's sons."},
{q:"Why were Barzillai's sons to eat at the king's table?", options:["They came to David when he fled because of Absalom","They funded the building of the temple","They fought the Philistines alone","They carried the ark to Jerusalem"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 2:7",verse:"But shew kindness unto the sons of Barzillai the Gileadite, and let them be of those that eat at thy table: for so they came to me when I fled because of Absalom thy brother.", insight:"Loyalty in the dark days earns a seat at the table; God repays faithfulness shown in exile."},
{q:"What had Shimei done to David?", options:["Cursed him with a grievous curse at Bahurim","Stoned him at Jerusalem","Betrayed him to Absalom","Stolen his crown"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 2:8",verse:"And, behold, thou hast with thee Shimei the son of Gera, a Benjamite of Bahurim, which cursed me with a grievous curse in the day when I went to Mahanaim: but he came down to meet me at Jordan, and I sware to him by the LORD, saying, I will not put thee to death with the sword.", insight:"A curse uttered in a king's humiliation is not forgotten in heaven; words have a long memory."},
{q:"What did David say must become of Shimei?", options:["Hold him not guiltless; bring his hoar head down to the grave with blood","Forgive him fully and forget","Banish him to Egypt","Make him a priest"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 2:9",verse:"Now therefore hold him not guiltless: for thou art a wise man, and knowest what thou oughtest to do unto him; but his hoar head bring thou down to the grave with blood.", insight:"David's oath had tied his own hands, but Solomon's were free; some debts pass to the next steward."},
{q:"How long did David reign over Israel?", options:["Forty years: seven in Hebron, and thirty-three in Jerusalem","Thirty years in all","Seventy years","Fifty years in Jerusalem"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 2:11",verse:"And the days that David reigned over Israel were forty years: seven years reigned he in Hebron, and thirty and three years reigned he in Jerusalem.", insight:"Forty years of reigning, then sleep with his fathers; every reign ends, but God's covenant marches on."},
{q:"What did Adonijah ask Bath-sheba to request for him?", options:["That Solomon give him Abishag the Shunammite to wife","The throne of Israel","Joab's command of the host","Land in the tribe of Judah"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 2:17",verse:"And he said, Speak, I pray thee, unto Solomon the king, (for he will not say thee nay,) that he give me Abishag the Shunammite to wife.", insight:"Asking for the king's attendant was asking for the kingdom; ambition hides in small petitions."},
{q:"How did Solomon receive his mother when she came?", options:["He rose to meet her, bowed to her, and set a seat for her at his right hand","He refused to see her","He met her at the city gate","He sent her away unheard"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 2:19",verse:"Bath-sheba therefore went unto king Solomon, to speak unto him for Adonijah. And the king rose up to meet her, and bowed himself unto her, and sat down on his throne, and caused a seat to be set for the king’s mother; and she sat on his right hand.", insight:"The wisest king on earth stood for his mother; honor to parents outranks even the throne."},
{q:"What did Solomon say of Adonijah's request?", options:["Ask for him the kingdom also","Grant it gladly","Consult the priests first","Give him a city instead"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 2:22",verse:"And king Solomon answered and said unto his mother, And why dost thou ask Abishag the Shunammite for Adonijah? ask for him the kingdom also; for he is mine elder brother; even for him, and for Abiathar the priest, and for Joab the son of Zeruiah.", insight:"Solomon saw through the small ask to the large ambition; wisdom reads the request behind the request."},
{q:"Who fell upon Adonijah that he died?", options:["Benaiah the son of Jehoiada","Joab the son of Zeruiah","Zadok the priest","Nathan the prophet"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 2:25",verse:"And king Solomon sent by the hand of Benaiah the son of Jehoiada; and he fell upon him that he died.", insight:"The sword David spared in chapter 1 fell in chapter 2; mercy refused becomes judgment invited."},
{q:"What became of Abiathar the priest?", options:["He was sent to his own fields at Anathoth, thrust out from being priest","He was made high priest","He was put to death","He was sent as envoy to Egypt"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 2:27",verse:"So Solomon thrust out Abiathar from being priest unto the LORD; that he might fulfil the word of the LORD, which he spake concerning the house of Eli in Shiloh.", insight:"God's old word against Eli's house stood firm; no office outlasts the word of the LORD."},
{q:"Why was Abiathar spared from death?", options:["He bore the ark of the Lord GOD before David, and was afflicted in all David's affliction","He was too old to punish","He fled the country in time","The people pleaded for him"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 2:26",verse:"And unto Abiathar the priest said the king, Get thee to Anathoth, unto thine own fields; for thou art worthy of death: but I will not at this time put thee to death, because thou barest the ark of the Lord GOD before David my father, and because thou hast been afflicted in all wherein my father was afflicted.", insight:"Shared suffering with God's anointed counts; Solomon honored the loyalty that had cost Abiathar."},
{q:"Where did Joab flee when tidings came to him?", options:["To the tabernacle of the LORD, catching hold on the horns of the altar","To Gath","To the wilderness","To Hebron"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 2:28",verse:"Then tidings came to Joab: for Joab had turned after Adonijah, though he turned not after Absalom. And Joab fled unto the tabernacle of the LORD, and caught hold on the horns of the altar.", insight:"The altar cannot shelter a murderer; Joab learned too late that refuge is for the penitent."},
{q:"Why did Solomon command Joab's death?", options:["To take away the innocent blood which Joab shed, from David's house","For treason against Israel","For stealing temple gold","For cursing the king"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 2:31",verse:"And the king said unto him, Do as he hath said, and fall upon him, and bury him; that thou mayest take away the innocent blood, which Joab shed, from me, and from the house of my father.", insight:"Innocent blood cries from the ground; a kingdom is cleansed only when justice is done."},
{q:"What boundary did Solomon set for Shimei?", options:["Build a house in Jerusalem and never leave; cross the brook Kidron and surely die","Pay a yearly tribute of gold","Serve in the temple","Never speak David's name"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 2:37",verse:"For it shall be, that on the day thou goest out, and passest over the brook Kidron, thou shalt know for certain that thou shalt surely die: thy blood shall be upon thine own head.", insight:"The terms were plain and the mercy was wide; Shimei's ruin was his own choice, not the king's harshness."},
{q:"How did Shimei break the oath?", options:["Two of his servants ran away to Gath, and he rode there to fetch them","He cursed Solomon openly","He joined a rebellion","He fled to Egypt"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 2:40",verse:"And Shimei arose, and saddled his ass, and went to Gath to Achish to seek his servants: and Shimei went, and brought his servants from Gath.", insight:"Two servants were worth more to him than his sworn word; small disobedience unmakes a man."}
]},
{n:3, name:"Solomon Asks for Wisdom", seal:{ref:"1 Kings 3:9",verse:"Give therefore thy servant an understanding heart to judge thy people, that I may discern between good and bad: for who is able to judge this thy so great a people?"}, facts:["Did you know Solomon offered a thousand burnt offerings on the altar at Gibeon before the LORD appeared to him in a dream by night (1 Kings 3:4-5)?","Did you know God promised Solomon a wise and understanding heart, 'so that there was none like thee before thee, neither after thee shall any arise like unto thee' (1 Kings 3:12)?","Did you know the famous judgment turned on one sentence: the true mother's bowels yearned upon her son, and she gave the child away to save its life (1 Kings 3:26)?"], questions:[
{q:"With whom did Solomon make affinity?", options:["Pharaoh king of Egypt, taking Pharaoh's daughter","Hiram king of Tyre","The king of Moab","The queen of Sheba"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 3:1",verse:"And Solomon made affinity with Pharaoh king of Egypt, and took Pharaoh’s daughter, and brought her into the city of David, until he had made an end of building his own house, and the house of the LORD, and the wall of Jerusalem round about.", insight:"A political marriage at the start of the reign; even wise beginnings can carry the seeds of later trouble."},
{q:"How did Solomon show his love for the LORD?", options:["Walking in the statutes of David his father","Building the temple at once","Destroying all the high places","Numbering the people of Israel"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 3:3",verse:"And Solomon loved the LORD, walking in the statutes of David his father: only he sacrificed and burnt incense in high places.", insight:"Love for God walked in a father's footsteps; the best inheritance is a pattern of obedience."},
{q:"Where was the great high place where Solomon sacrificed?", options:["Gibeon","Bethel","Hebron","Shiloh"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 3:4",verse:"And the king went to Gibeon to sacrifice there; for that was the great high place: a thousand burnt offerings did Solomon offer upon that altar.", insight:"Gibeon held the great altar; God meets extravagant worship even in imperfect places."},
{q:"How many burnt offerings did Solomon offer at Gibeon?", options:["A thousand","Seven","One hundred","Ten thousand"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 3:4",verse:"And the king went to Gibeon to sacrifice there; for that was the great high place: a thousand burnt offerings did Solomon offer upon that altar.", insight:"A thousand offerings before one dream; lavish worship opened the door to lavish wisdom."},
{q:"What did God say to Solomon in the dream at Gibeon?", options:["Ask what I shall give thee","Build me a house","Number my people","Go to war with Egypt"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 3:5",verse:"In Gibeon the LORD appeared to Solomon in a dream by night: and God said, Ask what I shall give thee.", insight:"God's question is God's test; what you ask for reveals what you are."},
{q:"How did Solomon describe himself to God?", options:["I am but a little child: I know not how to go out or come in","A mighty warrior in battle","A proven and tested king","Older and wiser than my father"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 3:7",verse:"And now, O LORD my God, thou hast made thy servant king instead of David my father: and I am but a little child: I know not how to go out or come in.", insight:"The king called himself a little child; humility before God is the doorway to wisdom."},
{q:"What did Solomon ask God to give him?", options:["An understanding heart to judge thy people, to discern between good and bad","Long life","Riches","The life of his enemies"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 3:9",verse:"Give therefore thy servant an understanding heart to judge thy people, that I may discern between good and bad: for who is able to judge this thy so great a people?", insight:"He asked for the tool of his calling, not the treasures of his comfort; ask for what your work needs."},
{q:"Why did Solomon's request please the Lord?", options:["He asked for understanding to discern judgment, not long life, riches, or his enemies' lives","He asked for the largest kingdom","He promised a greater temple","He vowed never to marry"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 3:11",verse:"And God said unto him, Because thou hast asked this thing, and hast not asked for thyself long life; neither hast asked riches for thyself, nor hast asked the life of thine enemies; but hast asked for thyself understanding to discern judgment;", insight:"God delights in unselfish asking; the prayer that serves others pleases heaven most."},
{q:"What did God promise about Solomon's wisdom?", options:["None like thee before thee, neither after thee shall any arise like unto thee","Greater than the angels","Equal to Moses only","Wiser than all the prophets"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 3:12",verse:"Behold, I have done according to thy words: lo, I have given thee a wise and an understanding heart; so that there was none like thee before thee, neither after thee shall any arise like unto thee.", insight:"A once-in-history gift for a once-given prayer; God is not stingy with the humble."},
{q:"What did God give Solomon besides wisdom, though unasked?", options:["Riches and honour, so that no king would be like him all his days","A longer life only","Victory over Egypt","Sons without number"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 3:13",verse:"And I have also given thee that which thou hast not asked, both riches, and honour: so that there shall not be any among the kings like unto thee all thy days.", insight:"Seek first the kingdom's need, and the extras follow; God adds what you did not ask."},
{q:"On what condition would God lengthen Solomon's days?", options:["If he would walk in God's ways and keep His statutes and commandments, as David did walk","If he built the temple in seven years","If he never took a wife","If he counted all Israel"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 3:14",verse:"And if thou wilt walk in my ways, to keep my statutes and my commandments, as thy father David did walk, then I will lengthen thy days.", insight:"Even unmatched wisdom came with a condition; gifts are kept by obedience."},
{q:"What did Solomon do when he awoke from the dream?", options:["He stood before the ark, offered burnt and peace offerings, and made a feast for his servants","He went back to sleep","He told the dream to Pharaoh","He built an altar at Gibeon"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 3:15",verse:"And Solomon awoke; and, behold, it was a dream. And he came to Jerusalem, and stood before the ark of the covenant of the LORD, and offered up burnt offerings, and offered peace offerings, and made a feast to all his servants.", insight:"He woke and worshiped; the right response to God's gift is gratitude, not pride."},
{q:"Who came to Solomon for judgment?", options:["Two women, that were harlots","Two elders of Israel","Two priests","Two captains of the host"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 3:16",verse:"Then came there two women, that were harlots, unto the king, and stood before him.", insight:"The king's wisdom was tested on the lowly first; God's wisdom serves the least before the greatest."},
{q:"What happened to one woman's child in the night?", options:["It died, because she overlaid it","It was stolen away","It fell gravely ill","It was taken by soldiers"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 3:19",verse:"And this woman’s child died in the night; because she overlaid it.", insight:"Carelessness in the night brought death by morning; small neglects carry heavy costs."},
{q:"What did the other woman do at midnight?", options:["She took the living son and laid her dead child in the first woman's bosom","She fled the house","She woke the neighbors","She called the city guards"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 3:20",verse:"And she arose at midnight, and took my son from beside me, while thine handmaid slept, and laid it in her bosom, and laid her dead child in my bosom.", insight:"Darkness loves a swap; the midnight exchange shows how deceit works while others sleep."},
{q:"What startling command did Solomon give?", options:["Bring me a sword. Divide the living child in two, and give half to the one, and half to the other","Stone them both","Cast lots for the child","Send the child to the priests"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 3:25",verse:"And the king said, Divide the living child in two, and give half to the one, and half to the other.", insight:"The sword was never meant to fall; sometimes wisdom threatens in order to reveal."},
{q:"What did the true mother say?", options:["O my lord, give her the living child, and in no wise slay it","Divide it equally","Give it to the priests","Cast lots for it"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 3:26",verse:"Then spake the woman whose the living child was unto the king, for her bowels yearned upon her son, and she said, O my lord, give her the living child, and in no wise slay it. But the other said, Let it be neither mine nor thine, but divide it.", insight:"True love would rather lose the child than see it die; selfless love gives up to save."},
{q:"What did the other woman say?", options:["Let it be neither mine nor thine, but divide it","She wept and withdrew","She confessed at once","She demanded witnesses"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 3:26",verse:"Then spake the woman whose the living child was unto the king, for her bowels yearned upon her son, and she said, O my lord, give her the living child, and in no wise slay it. But the other said, Let it be neither mine nor thine, but divide it.", insight:"'Neither mine nor thine' is the voice of envy; false love would rather destroy than lose."},
{q:"How did Solomon render the judgment?", options:["Give her the living child, and in no wise slay it: she is the mother thereof","He divided the child","He cast them both out","He gave the child to the priests"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 3:27",verse:"Then the king answered and said, Give her the living child, and in no wise slay it: she is the mother thereof.", insight:"The heart that would sacrifice itself proved itself the mother; love is known by what it surrenders."},
{q:"How did all Israel respond to the judgment?", options:["They feared the king, for they saw that the wisdom of God was in him, to do judgment","They rebelled against him","They laughed at the trick","They ignored the judgment"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 3:28",verse:"And all Israel heard of the judgment which the king had judged; and they feared the king: for they saw that the wisdom of God was in him, to do judgment.", insight:"A nation feared a just king; righteous judgment makes people reverent, not resentful."}
]},
{n:4, name:"The Glory of Solomon's Kingdom", seal:{ref:"1 Kings 4:25",verse:"And Judah and Israel dwelt safely, every man under his vine and under his fig tree, from Dan even to Beer-sheba, all the days of Solomon."}, facts:["Did you know Solomon's table required thirty measures of fine flour and sixty of meal every day, besides ten fat oxen, twenty pasture oxen, and a hundred sheep (1 Kings 4:22-23)?","Did you know Solomon kept forty thousand stalls of horses for his chariots, and twelve thousand horsemen (1 Kings 4:26)?","Did you know Solomon spoke three thousand proverbs, and his songs were a thousand and five, and he taught of trees, beasts, fowl, creeping things, and fishes (1 Kings 4:32-33)?"], questions:[
{q:"Who is named first among Solomon's princes?", options:["Azariah the son of Zadok the priest","Benaiah the son of Jehoiada","Nathan the prophet","Joab the son of Zeruiah"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 4:2",verse:"And these were the princes which he had; Azariah the son of Zadok the priest,", insight:"The priest's son heads the list; in Solomon's kingdom, worship came before warfare."},
{q:"Who were Solomon's scribes?", options:["Elihoreph and Ahiah, the sons of Shisha","The sons of Nathan","Zadok and Abiathar","Jehoshaphat and Azariah"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 4:3",verse:"Elihoreph and Ahiah, the sons of Shisha, scribes; Jehoshaphat the son of Ahilud, the recorder.", insight:"The kingdom ran on records; order in the scribes' room is order in the realm."},
{q:"Who was over the host?", options:["Benaiah the son of Jehoiada","Joab the son of Zeruiah","Abner the son of Ner","Amasa the son of Jether"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 4:4",verse:"And Benaiah the son of Jehoiada was over the host: and Zadok and Abiathar were the priests:", insight:"Loyalty outlasts talent; Benaiah the faithful replaced Joab the treacherous."},
{q:"Who was principal officer and the king's friend?", options:["Zabud the son of Nathan","Azariah the son of Nathan","Ahishar","Adoniram the son of Abda"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 4:5",verse:"And Azariah the son of Nathan was over the officers: and Zabud the son of Nathan was principal officer, and the king’s friend:", insight:"The prophet's son became the king's friend; godly counsel keeps its place near power."},
{q:"Who was over the tribute?", options:["Adoniram the son of Abda","Ahishar","Jehoshaphat the recorder","Geber the son of Uri"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 4:6",verse:"And Ahishar was over the household: and Adoniram the son of Abda was over the tribute.", insight:"Even tribute had its steward; prosperity needs faithful hands to gather and keep it."},
{q:"How many officers provided victuals for the king and his household?", options:["Twelve, each man his month in a year","Seven","Thirty","Seventy"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 4:7",verse:"And Solomon had twelve officers over all Israel, which provided victuals for the king and his household: each man his month in a year made provision.", insight:"Twelve officers, twelve months, no one crushed; shared burdens keep a kingdom fed."},
{q:"Which officer had Taphath the daughter of Solomon to wife?", options:["The son of Abinadab, in all the region of Dor","Ahimaaz in Naphtali","Baana the son of Ahilud","Ahinadab the son of Iddo"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 4:11",verse:"The son of Abinadab, in all the region of Dor; which had Taphath the daughter of Solomon to wife:", insight:"The king bound his officers to himself by marriage; wisdom weaves loyalty into the family."},
{q:"Which officer took Basmath the daughter of Solomon to wife?", options:["Ahimaaz, in Naphtali","The son of Hur, in mount Ephraim","Shimei the son of Elah, in Benjamin","Jehoshaphat the son of Paruah, in Issachar"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 4:15",verse:"Ahimaaz was in Naphtali; he also took Basmath the daughter of Solomon to wife:", insight:"A daughter given in Naphtali; the kingdom's edges were held by covenant, not only by force."},
{q:"How are Judah and Israel described in Solomon's days?", options:["Many, as the sand by the sea in multitude, eating and drinking, and making merry","Few and fearful","Scattered in exile","Hungry and at war"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 4:20",verse:"Judah and Israel were many, as the sand which is by the sea in multitude, eating and drinking, and making merry.", insight:"Multitude and merriment under a wise king; God's blessing shows in a joyful people."},
{q:"Over what did Solomon reign?", options:["All kingdoms from the river unto the land of the Philistines, and unto the border of Egypt","Only the tribe of Judah","From Egypt to Assyria","The isles of the sea"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 4:21",verse:"And Solomon reigned over all kingdoms from the river unto the land of the Philistines, and unto the border of Egypt: they brought presents, and served Solomon all the days of his life.", insight:"From the river to Egypt's border; God stretched the promise wider than any king before."},
{q:"What was Solomon's daily provision of fine flour?", options:["Thirty measures","Ten measures","One hundred measures","Sixty measures"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 4:22",verse:"And Solomon’s provision for one day was thirty measures of fine flour, and threescore measures of meal,", insight:"Thirty measures a day for one table; abundance is God's signature on a faithful reign."},
{q:"How many sheep were provided for one day?", options:["An hundred","Ten","Fifty","A thousand"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 4:23",verse:"Ten fat oxen, and twenty oxen out of the pastures, and an hundred sheep, beside harts, and roebucks, and fallowdeer, and fatted fowl.", insight:"A hundred sheep a day; the king's table fed multitudes, not just the crown."},
{q:"What game and fowl came to the table besides oxen and sheep?", options:["Harts, and roebucks, and fallowdeer, and fatted fowl","Camels and horses","Fish and honey","Olives and wine"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 4:23",verse:"Ten fat oxen, and twenty oxen out of the pastures, and an hundred sheep, beside harts, and roebucks, and fallowdeer, and fatted fowl.", insight:"The forest and the field both served the king; creation itself provisioned Solomon's house."},
{q:"How is the safety of Solomon's reign pictured?", options:["Every man under his vine and under his fig tree, from Dan even to Beer-sheba","Behind walls of brass","In chariots of iron","In caves and strongholds"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 4:25",verse:"And Judah and Israel dwelt safely, every man under his vine and under his fig tree, from Dan even to Beer-sheba, all the days of Solomon.", insight:"Vine and fig tree, Dan to Beer-sheba; true peace is a man at rest under his own shade."},
{q:"How many stalls of horses did Solomon have for his chariots?", options:["Forty thousand","Twelve thousand","Four thousand","One thousand"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 4:26",verse:"And Solomon had forty thousand stalls of horses for his chariots, and twelve thousand horsemen.", insight:"Forty thousand stalls; strength multiplied, yet the wise king's true defense was God."},
{q:"How many horsemen did Solomon have?", options:["Twelve thousand","Forty thousand","Three thousand","Seventy thousand"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 4:26",verse:"And Solomon had forty thousand stalls of horses for his chariots, and twelve thousand horsemen.", insight:"Twelve thousand horsemen stood ready; power is a tool, and tools must serve the right master."},
{q:"What did God give Solomon besides wisdom and understanding?", options:["Largeness of heart, even as the sand on the sea shore","Gold without measure","Victory in every battle","Life without end"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 4:29",verse:"And God gave Solomon wisdom and understanding exceeding much, and largeness of heart, even as the sand that is on the sea shore.", insight:"A heart as large as the seashore's sand; wisdom without largeness of heart is a small gift."},
{q:"Solomon was wiser than all men, including whom?", options:["Ethan the Ezrahite, and Heman, and Chalcol, and Darda, the sons of Mahol","David and Moses","Joseph and Daniel","Adam and Noah"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 4:31",verse:"For he was wiser than all men; than Ethan the Ezrahite, and Heman, and Chalcol, and Darda, the sons of Mahol: and his fame was in all nations round about.", insight:"Named and outshone, the sages of the age; God's gift needs no rivals, only gratitude."},
{q:"How many proverbs did Solomon speak?", options:["Three thousand","One thousand","Seven hundred","Ten thousand"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 4:32",verse:"And he spake three thousand proverbs: and his songs were a thousand and five.", insight:"Three thousand proverbs from one wise heart; wisdom shared multiplies beyond counting."},
{q:"How many were Solomon's songs?", options:["A thousand and five","One hundred and fifty","Seven","Three thousand"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 4:32",verse:"And he spake three thousand proverbs: and his songs were a thousand and five.", insight:"A thousand and five songs; the wisest man sang, for wisdom without worship is incomplete."}
]},
{n:5, name:"Timber from Tyre", seal:{ref:"1 Kings 5:5",verse:"And, behold, I purpose to build an house unto the name of the LORD my God, as the LORD spake unto David my father, saying, Thy son, whom I will set upon thy throne in thy room, he shall build an house unto my name."}, facts:["Did you know Hiram king of Tyre is described as one who 'was ever a lover of David,' and he rejoiced greatly when Solomon's message came (1 Kings 5:1, 7)?","Did you know the cedar timber traveled from Lebanon to the building site by sea, lashed into floats and discharged at an appointed port (1 Kings 5:9)?","Did you know Solomon's building force numbered thirty thousand levy men, seventy thousand burden bearers, eighty thousand hewers, and three thousand three hundred officers ruling the work (1 Kings 5:13-16)?"], questions:[
{q:"Who sent his servants to Solomon?", options:["Hiram king of Tyre","Pharaoh king of Egypt","The king of Moab","Achish king of Gath"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 5:1",verse:"And Hiram king of Tyre sent his servants unto Solomon; for he had heard that they had anointed him king in the room of his father: for Hiram was ever a lover of David.", insight:"Tyre's king came first to Solomon; honor given to the father's friend becomes honor to the son."},
{q:"Why did Hiram send to Solomon?", options:["He heard they had anointed him king in his father's room; for Hiram was ever a lover of David","To demand tribute from Israel","To declare war on Judah","To buy horses for his chariots"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 5:1",verse:"And Hiram king of Tyre sent his servants unto Solomon; for he had heard that they had anointed him king in the room of his father: for Hiram was ever a lover of David.", insight:"'Ever a lover of David'; old friendships are a treasure a new king should honor."},
{q:"Why could David not build a house for the LORD?", options:["For the wars which were about him on every side, until the LORD put them under his feet","He lacked the timber","The priests forbade it","He had no sons to help"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 5:3",verse:"Thou knowest how that David my father could not build an house unto the name of the LORD his God for the wars which were about him on every side, until the LORD put them under the soles of his feet.", insight:"The warrior's hands were too bloody for the temple; God assigns the building to the man of peace."},
{q:"What rest did the LORD give Solomon?", options:["Rest on every side, so that there was neither adversary nor evil occurrent","Wealth without measure","Armies without number","Peace only in Judah"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 5:4",verse:"But now the LORD my God hath given me rest on every side, so that there is neither adversary nor evil occurrent.", insight:"Rest on every side is God's gift, not man's achievement; peace is the platform for building."},
{q:"What did Solomon purpose to build?", options:["An house unto the name of the LORD his God","A palace greater than Pharaoh's","A wall around the city of Tyre","A temple to the sun"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 5:5",verse:"And, behold, I purpose to build an house unto the name of the LORD my God, as the LORD spake unto David my father, saying, Thy son, whom I will set upon thy throne in thy room, he shall build an house unto my name.", insight:"A house for God's name, not Solomon's; the noblest building serves Another's glory."},
{q:"What had the LORD given Solomon on every side?", options:["Rest, with neither adversary nor evil occurrent","War with every neighbor","Famine throughout the land","A fleet ready for Tarshish"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 5:4",verse:"But now the LORD my God hath given me rest on every side, so that there is neither adversary nor evil occurrent.", insight:"Rest before the work; God quiets the borders before He raises the house."},
{q:"What timber did Solomon ask Hiram to hew?", options:["Cedar trees out of Lebanon","Oak from Bashan","Shittim from the desert","Cypress from Cyprus"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 5:6",verse:"Now therefore command thou that they hew me cedar trees out of Lebanon; and my servants shall be with thy servants: and unto thee will I give hire for thy servants according to all that thou shalt appoint: for thou knowest that there is not among us any that can skill to hew timber like unto the Sidonians.", insight:"Lebanon's cedars for God's house; the best materials belong in the best service."},
{q:"Who alone could skill to hew timber?", options:["The Sidonians","The Egyptians","The Israelites","The men of Tyre"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 5:6",verse:"Now therefore command thou that they hew me cedar trees out of Lebanon; and my servants shall be with thy servants: and unto thee will I give hire for thy servants according to all that thou shalt appoint: for thou knowest that there is not among us any that can skill to hew timber like unto the Sidonians.", insight:"Solomon admitted what his people could not do; wisdom hires the skill it lacks."},
{q:"How did Hiram receive Solomon's words?", options:["He rejoiced greatly, and blessed the LORD for giving David a wise son","He refused outright","He demanded gold first","He wept with fear"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 5:7",verse:"And it came to pass, when Hiram heard the words of Solomon, that he rejoiced greatly, and said, Blessed be the LORD this day, which hath given unto David a wise son over this great people.", insight:"A Gentile king blessed the LORD; God's wisdom in His servant draws praise from strangers."},
{q:"What timber would Hiram supply?", options:["Timber of cedar, and timber of fir","Cedar and oak","Fir and pine only","Shittim and cedar"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 5:8",verse:"And Hiram sent to Solomon, saying, I have considered the things which thou sentest to me for: and I will do all thy desire concerning timber of cedar, and concerning timber of fir.", insight:"Cedar and fir, all Solomon desired; God moves foreign kings to furnish His house."},
{q:"How would the timber be brought from Lebanon?", options:["Hiram's servants would bring it down to the sea and convey it by sea in floats","Carried overland on camels","Dragged by oxen through the hills","Floated down the Jordan"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 5:9",verse:"My servants shall bring them down from Lebanon unto the sea: and I will convey them by sea in floats unto the place that thou shalt appoint me, and will cause them to be discharged there, and thou shalt receive them: and thou shalt accomplish my desire, in giving food for my household.", insight:"Floats on the sea for a temple on the hill; God provides strange roads for holy timber."},
{q:"What did Hiram desire in return?", options:["Food for his household","Gold and silver","Solomon's daughters in marriage","Cities in Galilee"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 5:9",verse:"My servants shall bring them down from Lebanon unto the sea: and I will convey them by sea in floats unto the place that thou shalt appoint me, and will cause them to be discharged there, and thou shalt receive them: and thou shalt accomplish my desire, in giving food for my household.", insight:"Bread for timber, an honest trade; fair dealing between kings honors both."},
{q:"What did Solomon give Hiram year by year?", options:["Twenty thousand measures of wheat for food, and twenty measures of pure oil","Ten thousand talents of gold","A hundred oxen","Cedar from Israel"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 5:11",verse:"And Solomon gave Hiram twenty thousand measures of wheat for food to his household, and twenty measures of pure oil: thus gave Solomon to Hiram year by year.", insight:"Year by year, without fail; covenants are kept by steady giving, not grand gestures."},
{q:"What was between Hiram and Solomon?", options:["Peace; and they two made a league together","A marriage alliance","A pact of war","A trade embargo"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 5:12",verse:"And the LORD gave Solomon wisdom, as he promised him: and there was peace between Hiram and Solomon; and they two made a league together.", insight:"Peace sealed with a league; the house of God rose on a foundation of peace."},
{q:"How large was the levy Solomon raised out of Israel?", options:["Thirty thousand men","Three thousand","Seventy thousand","Three hundred thousand"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 5:13",verse:"And king Solomon raised a levy out of all Israel; and the levy was thirty thousand men.", insight:"Thirty thousand hands for God's house; great work gathers many workers."},
{q:"How were the levy men rotated at Lebanon?", options:["Ten thousand a month by courses: a month in Lebanon, and two months at home","All year in Lebanon without rest","Six months each without relief","By lot, with no time at home"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 5:14",verse:"And he sent them to Lebanon ten thousand a month by courses: a month they were in Lebanon, and two months at home: and Adoniram was over the levy.", insight:"A month of labor, two months at home; even sacred work must not devour the worker."},
{q:"Who was over the levy?", options:["Adoniram","Ahishar","Benaiah","Zabud"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 5:14",verse:"And he sent them to Lebanon ten thousand a month by courses: a month they were in Lebanon, and two months at home: and Adoniram was over the levy.", insight:"The tribute master now led the levy; faithful stewards rise to greater trusts."},
{q:"How many burden bearers and hewers did Solomon have?", options:["Threescore and ten thousand burden bearers, and fourscore thousand hewers in the mountains","Ten thousand of each","Thirty thousand of each","Three thousand and three hundred"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 5:15",verse:"And Solomon had threescore and ten thousand that bare burdens, and fourscore thousand hewers in the mountains;", insight:"One hundred and fifty thousand laborers; no one builds for God alone, and no labor is unseen."},
{q:"How many officers ruled over the people that wrought?", options:["Three thousand and three hundred","Twelve","Seventy","Thirty thousand"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 5:16",verse:"Beside the chief of Solomon’s officers which were over the work, three thousand and three hundred, which ruled over the people that wrought in the work.", insight:"Overseers for every rank; God's work deserves order, not confusion."},
{q:"What stones did the king command for the foundation?", options:["Great stones, costly stones, and hewed stones","Common field stones","Bricks of clay","Marble from Egypt"], a:0, ref:"1 Kings 5:17",verse:"And the king commanded, and they brought great stones, costly stones, and hewed stones, to lay the foundation of the house.", insight:"Costly stones for the foundation, unseen by most; God values what is hidden as much as what is shown."}
]}
]);
